Disable Microsoft build of Go toolchain telemetry by default through go.env

Microsoft build of Go 1.26.10-1 reads MS_GOTOOLCHAIN_TELEMETRY_ENABLED through Go's
standard configuration. Set the installed default to 0 while preserving
opt-in through go env -w MS_GOTOOLCHAIN_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=1 or the environment.
The upstream script harness already enables telemetry for its fake endpoint,
so no Go code or test changes are needed.

This does not affect the separate upstream Go telemetry, which defaults to
"local" mode and uploads nothing unless the user runs `go telemetry on`.
---
--- a/go.env
+++ b/go.env
@@ -10,4 +10,4 @@
-# Enable telemetry in the Microsoft build of Go by default. Users can opt out by
-# setting MS_GOTOOLCHAIN_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=0 in their environment or with go env -w.
+# Disable telemetry in the Microsoft build of Go by default. Users can opt in by
+# setting MS_GOTOOLCHAIN_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=1 in their environment or with go env -w.
 # See https://github.com/microsoft/go/blob/microsoft/main/eng/doc/Telemetry.md.
-MS_GOTOOLCHAIN_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=1
+MS_GOTOOLCHAIN_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=0
